  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full 111-minute set at the 40 Watt Club in Athens, Georgia on Saturday, May 30, 2026 [1][2]. This is the 459th show in the archive's collection for the band, following a performance the previous day at the Neighborhood Theatre [2]. The recording, captured by soundboard engineer Kyle Kennelly and transferred by him and Emerald Green, is the only available audio for this date [1]. The setlist features a mix of deep cuts and fan favorites, including rare tracks like “Armies of the Lord,” “Need More Bandages,” and “Dawn of Revelation” [1][2]. Several songs are notable bustouts, such as “Onions,” which had not been played in 64 archived shows, and “Good Morning to All Vultures,” a mythic rarity with only two archived performances [2]. The band also played “Isaiah 45 23,” “Genesis 3 23,” and “Your Bandage,” all of which are considered rare in the archive [2]. The show included spoken introductions for “No Children” and an abridged version of the “Overture” [1]. The lineup concluded with “Up the Wolves” and “No Children” [1]. The tape includes banter between songs and a specific appreciation segment for a member named Wurster [1]. The uploader thanks the band and their management for supporting live taping efforts [1]. This recording offers a complete view of the night's musical journey, from the opening “Armies of the Lord” to the final “No Children” [1][2].",
